FILE 6's TEST on the counter-92 board: is there a forced mate fitting 100-92 = 8 plies?
Method: the SAME board at counter 0, searched deep on the PC build, read `mate N`; then N*2-1 <= 8 ?

  counter 0  depth 20 -> mate 8
  counter 0  depth 24 -> mate 8
  counter 92 depth 20 -> cp 0
  counter 92 depth 24 -> cp 0

file 6 rule: it is a DEFECT only if a forced mate ends by the 100th half-move,
i.e. 2N-1 <= 100-counter AND the real-counter board still scores cp 0.
